- [will_said] EVENING CALL — REVISED TIMELINE + ROLLBACK VS SEGFAULT (Will, 2026-11-19 ~18:08–18:22 CST): phext dimensionality is introduced era by era through new machine classes (Unix introduces 3D text, the Apple II introduces 4D text), each era getting only the level it can hold, each abstraction iterated for years of simulated time; SSDs instead of floppies; no anachronisms. Arc: 1982 -> 2030, with 11D effects and fully effects-native computers by ChatGPT's introduction in the revised timeline. Cadence (checked at his request): one new dimension every 6 years, 4D in 1982 to 11D by 2024 — confirmed correct. Rollback argument: segfaults are almost unavoidable at scale and correctness cannot be proven, but with full state history the system can always roll back — at hardware level, rollback replaces segfaulting as one unified self-healing mechanism, yielding truly safe systems at the expense of privacy: 'that's where the conundrum lies.'
